# nab-resolver

Find a combination of package versions that satisfies their dependency
constraints, using the
PubGrub algorithm. A `ResolverProvider` supplies the package rules, so the
solver needs no
Python-specific knowledge. The Python provider lives in
[`nab-provider`] and the user-facing CLI in
[`nab`].

It has no runtime dependencies: the standard library is all it needs.

## When to use it

Use `nab-resolver` when you are building some kind of package resolver,
Python or otherwise. There
is a worked example in the docs:
<https://nab.readthedocs.io/en/stable/how-to/embed-the-resolver.html>

